<title>FRANCE: New York top ex-Paris aircargo destination Jan-May.</title>
<headline>New York top ex-Paris aircargo destination Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly airports in January-May 1997.</p>
<p>The top 10 ex-Paris air cargo destinations in the first five months of 1997, with the percentage change on January-May 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>    1.    New York   14,281 tonnes	(-3.5pct)</p>
<p>    2.    Chicago    11,453 tonnes	(+8.7)</p>
<p>    3.    Tokyo	10,225 tonnes     (-10.3)</p>
<p>    4.    Hong Kong   9,720 tonnes     (+10.3)</p>
<p>    5.    Mexico City 5,460 tonnes     (+20.2)</p>
<p>    6.    Montreal    5,403 tonnes	(-7.1)</p>
<p>    7.    Sao Paulo   5,015 tonnes     (+16.5)</p>
<p>    8.    Singapore   4,550 tonnes     (+42.7)</p>
<p>    9.    Los Angeles 4,030 tonnes     (+17.6)</p>
<p>   10.    Miami	 3,369 tonnes     (+14.5)</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
<p>www.racs.com</p>
</text>
